course: dictionary
lesson: 14155
title: When words come out wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word misspoke is made of two parts: mis- means wrong, and spoke means said. So misspoke means said something wrongly. Mis- also appears in misread, misspell and misunderstand.
explain: Often it is an accident. «Sam meant to say seven, but he misspoke and said eleven.» The wrong word slipped out by mistake, and Sam did not mean it.
explain: Officials and politicians use misspoke in another way. «The minister said the school was open. Later she said, "I misspoke."» Here the words «later» and «take back» are the clues: she said something untrue or wrong, and she is trying to take it back without saying she lied.
fact: Misspoke means said something wrong, often by accident.
fact: Misspoke is the past tense of misspeak. Other forms are misspeaks and misspoken, as in «she has misspoken».
fact: In official talk, misspoke can mean said something untrue, often to avoid admitting a lie.
fact: «Misspoke» means said the wrong word by accident, as in «He misspoke and said eleven instead of seven.»
fact: A good check is to swap in «said something wrong» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Sam meant to say seven, but he misspoke and said eleven.» What does misspoke mean here? | *Said the wrong word by accident | Forgot to speak at all | Sang the answer | Said the right word very loudly
exercise: The minister said the school was open, then said, «I misspoke.» What is she probably trying to do? | Close the school | *Take back something wrong she said | Thank everyone for the school | Repeat the same words louder
exercise: Find and copy the past tense of misspeak. | speak | misspeaks | misspeak | *misspoke
test: Ella says, «I misspoke when I said the library was closed.» What does misspoke mean here? | *Said something wrong | Read a book | Locked the door | Sang a song
test: Which sentence shows a word coming out wrong by accident? | «She misspoke a happy song.» | «I misspoke my lunch in the bin.» | «The team misspoke and won the match.» | *«Oops, I misspoke: I said cat when I meant hat.»
exam: Mia says, «I misspoke», after the mayor's claim is shown to be false. What is most likely true? | *She said something untrue and is taking it back | She forgot her lines in the play by accident | She said the right word very loudly | She spelled a word wrongly on paper
